# Pinned Aether toolchain versions for CI — the single place to bump.
#
# aeb tags are "later means later" markers, NOT semver promises; pin them so a
# CI run is reproducible. `ci/toolchain.sh` reads these; override at the shell to
# test a bump (e.g. `AETHER_REF=v0.591.0 ci/run.sh`).

# The Aether compiler (`ae`). Tag vX.Y.Z, branch, or commit SHA.
# Pinned to 0.666.0, which is what aeb v0.309 itself pins (aeb e348bca "raise
# AETHER_PIN and AETHER_FETCH to 0.666.0") — keep the pair matched, since aeb
# builds its own tools with the ae it pins.
#
# The FLOOR remains 0.638.0: it carries the WebSocket client the BiDi work needs
# (std.http.ws_connect, first in 0.590 — see docs/WebDriver-BiDi.md) AND the
# single-file-module fix (aether aeec9b69 + a34ec231, "Accept single-file modules
# in [package] modules") that this repo's aether.toml [package] modules line
# depends on: `ae add github.com/aether-lang-dev/selaenium@<tag>` + `import
# webdriver` resolves with NO --lib only on >=0.638.0 (on 0.637.0 it was wrongly
# rejected as "does not exist").
#
# Verified on 0.666.0: the engine .so (49 exports), the grid hub + its probe, and
# the python/ruby/js/java/go/rust/dotnet/nim/d binding suites.
# Raised 0.666.0 -> 0.668.0 (2026-09-14). Newest published aether. Verified here:
# the engine builds to the same 49 exports, and grid/crystal/d/java/go/rust/python
# are green on it. aeb's own AETHER_PIN is still 0.666.0, which is a FLOOR
# ("anything newer on PATH is accepted as-is"), so the pair is still consistent.
#
# Raised 0.668.0 -> 0.675.0 (2026-09-15) — a REQUIRED move, coupled to AEB_REF
# v0.311. aeb v0.311 raised its own AETHER_PIN to 0.675.0 because its SDK modules
# now import std.strarr (0.675, PR #2034) + call fs.make_temp_dir/remove_tree/
# make_temp_file (0.670) to replace shell-outs — so the ae that compiles aeb's
# generated node files must be >= 0.675, or `aeb <node>` fails with
# `unresolved import 'std.strarr'` / `Undefined function 'fs.make_temp_dir'`.
# (Install trap: `ci/toolchain.sh` may drop 0.675 BINARIES without the version
# tree; `ae version install 0.675.0 && ae version use 0.675.0` installs the std.)
# Verified here on ae 0.675 + aeb v0.311: engine builds, and c/cpp/d/ruby nodes
# are green (1/1, 1/1, 2/2, 1/1).
#
# History: 0.677 shipped a whole-program codegen bug — a fixed
# imported_namespaces[64] cap silently dropped the 65th+ namespace, so a merged
# --emit=lib unit past 64 namespaces failed with a spurious
#   error[E0301]: Undefined function 'sha1.free_ctx'
# (a compiler-generated Sha1Ctx cleanup reached through the std.http/crypto
# graph). We held at 0.675 (folding .side playback into shell.ae to stay under
# the count). Fixed in aether PR #2045 — the namespace tables now grow
# dynamically, cap gone — released in 0.678.0.
#
# Raised 0.675.0 -> 0.678.0 (2026-09-16). Verified on the RELEASED 0.678 binary
# (a fresh `ae version install 0.678.0` fetch, not the local build): fresh engine
# .so build clean, adding an extra module no longer trips E0301, and .side
# playback moved back out of shell.ae into its own side_run.ae module. Full
# matrix green (engine 60 unit + slice; py 66/66, rust 1/1, go 1/1, D 2/2).
#
# Raised 0.678.0 -> 0.680.0 (2026-09-16). 0.680 ships the FreeBSD --emit=lib
# cross fixes (aether #2047 -shared/-fPIC on the link + #2049 -fPIC on the runtime
# object compiles), which unblock the freebsd-x86_64 engine leg — now built
# cleanly through release/build.sh and on the v0.8.0 release (byte-identical sha
# f605f53f… whether cut from the ahead-of-release #2049 build or the published
# 0.680, so provenance is clean). Verified on the RELEASED 0.680 binary: native
# engine + 60 unit tests green; d 2/2, go 1/1, rust 1/1, c 1/1.
#
# Raised 0.680.0 -> 0.681.0 (2026-09-17). 0.681 adds ONLY os.arch() (aether
# #2051) — the compile-time CPU-arch companion to os.platform(), returning the
# normalized ecosystem token (x86_64 never amd64, arm64 never aarch64). This lets
# selenium_core/.getFromGitHubReleases.ae drop its last shell-out (a single
# `uname -m`): the engine-fetch node now builds the release-asset name from
# os.platform() + "-" + os.arch(), no spawn, and correct under cross-fetch (the
# TARGET arch, which uname -m on the build host could not give). Consistent with
# aeb v0.314, whose AETHER_PIN 0.680.0 is a FLOOR (newer ae on PATH accepted):
# 0.681 > 0.680, so no coupled AEB_REF move. Verified on the RELEASED 0.681
# binary.
AETHER_REF=v0.681.0

# The aeb build runner. Tag v0.NNN, branch, or commit SHA.
#
# v0.309 closes BOTH of the aeb bugs this repo filed in asks/:
#   - v0.308 2734bf5 "nine test runners reported PASS on a failing suite (`| tee`
#     ate the exit code)" — our asks/aeb-missing-toolchain-reports-tests-passed.md.
#     A node whose compiler was missing used to report `tests PASSED`; it now
#     reddens. Re-verified here: d/.tests.ae with a dmd that always fails goes
#     from "2/2 PASS" to "0/1 FAIL".
#   - v0.309 72db50c + f05035d: aeb-resolve.jar is built as a single fat jar and
#     PUBLISHED AS A RELEASE ASSET, fetched by binary installs — our
#     asks/aeb-binary-release-omits-aeb-resolve-jar.md. v0.308 938faa9 also stops
#     `make install` wiping it, which is what had broken java/scala here.
#
# Also in v0.308: scala.scalac_test can scope discovery with
# source_layout("maven idiomatic"), and a groovyc cache-key fix (an empty argfile
# meant edited Groovy never rebuilt).
#
# Carried forward: v0.307 cpp dep-object linking (REQUIRED by cpp/, which links
# the C client's selenium.c compiled AS C so its extern "C" symbols aren't
# C++-mangled) + java.package_jar from_classes(); v0.306 rbenv() as a bare flag
# (ruby/.tests.ae declares it); v0.303 the tool-named Ruby SDK (ruby.bundle{} /
# ruby.gem{}); v0.300 the x86_64 arch word (assets aeb-<os>-x86_64.tar.gz,
# bldr._host_os_arch()), which ci/toolchain.sh, the crossbuild lib names, the jar
# /native/<os>-<arch>/ paths and Native.osArch() all track.
# Raised v0.309 -> v0.310 (2026-09-14). v0.310 pins ae 0.668.0 itself, so the
# pair is matched again. It carries the fixes for both asks this repo filed:
#   0959a64 scala: scalac_test fails loud on an EMPTY compiler classpath
#   e67de23 python: pip()/requirements_file() at top level fail loud — though
#           the root cause there was OURS (pip() is a block setter of
#           install()); python/.tests.ae was fixed and is 65/65.
# Also pre-fetches aeb-resolve.jar on install, so JVM bindings resolve offline.
#
# NOT everything is fixed: scalac_test still splices env() into the COMPILER
# classpath slot on v0.310 (`java -cp 'SELENIUM_CORE_LIB=…' dotty.tools.dotc.Main`),
# so scala/.tests.ae is still red. Re-filed as
# ../aeb/asks/scalac-test-env-prefix-lands-in-the-compiler-classpath.md.
#
# Raised v0.311 -> v0.312 (2026-09-16). v0.312 raised AETHER_PIN/AETHER_FETCH to
# 0.677.0 (see the AETHER_REF note above — this is a coupled pin). Install via the
# prebuilt platform bundle (aeb-linux-x86_64.tar.gz + .sha256, copy-only
# install.sh, no compiler needed). Engine + D suites verified green on the pair.
#
# Raised v0.312 -> v0.314 (2026-09-17). v0.314 brings --overrideDep (v0.313: node
# SUBSTITUTION — relabel a dep() edge to a substitute .ae producer) PLUS the read-
# redirect fix (v0.314: _read_dep_artifact follows the substitution, so a
# consumer's dep_artifact("<real>",key) transparently gets the substitute's
# published value). Together these make selenium_core/.getFromGitHubReleases.ae
# consumable: `aeb <target> --overrideDep selenium_core/.build.ae=selenium_core/.getFromGitHubReleases.ae`
# supplies the FETCHED prebuilt engine with no Aether toolchain. Not a coupled
# move — v0.314's AETHER_PIN is 0.680.0, matching our AETHER_REF. Verified on the
# RELEASED v0.314 (prebuilt bundle) + ae 0.680: engine 60 unit + matrix (d 2/2,
# go 1/1, rust 1/1, c 1/1) green; --overrideDep relabels + the substitute node
# publishes the engine. NB (fallback-masking caveat): a binding pass under
# --overrideDep isn't itself proof the override PATH won — the dep_artifact-layer
# resolution is; see asks/aeb-overridedep-does-not-redirect-dep-artifact-reads.md.
AEB_REF=v0.314
